WEBVTT

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:08.339
The Irresponsible Captain
Tylor

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:11.978
We may be off the maps...
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:14.037
...but let's stay on this voyage.
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:19.011
I will be holding, never let you go.

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:23.423
Whatever we may want...
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:25.550
...we'll take as we need.
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:30.352
So let's just go wherever we please!
Omoi no Mama Yukou!

00:00:32.064 --> 00:00:34.834
Make me your partner...
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:37.462
...on this journey.
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:41.332
One that you trust more than words!
Michizure ni Shite

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:47.439
Come on now and sail away for future!
Imasugu sail away for future

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:49.949
Things are waiting...
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:53.146
...that we've never seen before!
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:57.156
Just take your cares...
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:00:57.156 --> 00:01:01.217
...and throw them all away.
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:06.091
Come together, just think of tomorrow.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.357
Let's go!

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:16.005
FOR HIS WAS A GENIUS
NO RULE COULD CONTAIN

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:34.894
The new cruiser, Aso, on which
the United Planets Space Force...

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:37.829
...has concentrated its prestige
and the cream of its technology.

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:39.294
And...

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:47.240
On the other hand, the old
destroyer that existed only...

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.801
...to house soldiers with
a past. The Soyokaze.

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:53.808
It was never a very
well-equipped ship...

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.942
...but, instead, it had a
freedom no other one had.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:00.914
Seeing it being scrapped
like this makes me sad.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:02.284
Really?

00:02:03.055 --> 00:02:06.081
You left without really saying why,
but you still ended up here.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:09.089
Walking around on the ground till
I'm tired isn't fun anymore...

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:12.131
...and I'm not old enough
that having fun tires me out.

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:15.589
And even if everyone had a past,
it was everyone's ship.

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:19.733
I was exactly like everyone else.
I just happened to be the captain.

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:23.166
It's not too late.
The Aso's waiting for you.

00:02:23.809 --> 00:02:25.674
The Aso needs that freedom.

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:29.172
But, Yuriko... Freedom was nothing
but trouble for you, right?

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:31.977
So, who should get the freedom
and who the responsibility?

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:33.474
I had to break away.

00:02:33.886 --> 00:02:34.910
Break away?

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:37.356
Yeah, break away.

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:39.525
But, no matter how much
I break from something...

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.288
...I won't look
back or have regrets.

00:02:42.094 --> 00:02:44.858
So, you have no intention
of going onto the Aso?

00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:47.631
But... It's a military
ship, isn't it?

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.098
Captain...

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.300
Captain, have you changed?

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:56.975
Join me?

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:04.108
You're really something.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:32.310
I think this is the first time we've
ever had a drink alone like this.

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:35.672
It's not the alcohol that's
making my heart beat so fast.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:39.675
I don't want to go back.

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:42.280
Not to how I was
before I met you.

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:50.787
Oh, did you tell Mr. Yamamoto
and the others about me?

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:55.434
Yes. I think they're all going
half crazy looking for you now.

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:56.298
I see...

00:03:57.703 --> 00:03:59.762
I wonder why they'd bother?

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:04.371
They shouldn't waste their
time looking for me.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.675
But, they're all
worried about you.

00:04:13.185 --> 00:04:15.710
You've decided to take that
ground duty, haven't you?

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:19.947
Doing what you think you
should do is the best thing.

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:22.993
The same goes for
Mr. Yamamoto and the others.

00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:27.025
You only live once, so don't live
according to someone else's rules.

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.699
Do what you want
the way you want to.

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:32.235
What we want?

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.434
What you want.

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:44.778
Yuriko, if you see Mr. Yamamoto
and the others, tell them that.

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:48.544
Okay?

00:04:56.862 --> 00:05:01.663
You did it over and over
and over and over again...

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:03.833
You fooled us all.

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:08.105
Captain, I... I'm going back.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.501
Huh? Right now?

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:14.942
Yes. When I get back, I'll
tell them all what you told me.

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:18.315
To do what they want
the way they want to.

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:23.812
But don't you think they've
figured that out themselves by now?

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:27.159
They're looking for you
because they haven't.

00:05:27.159 --> 00:05:29.218
That's why I'm going back.

00:05:42.341 --> 00:05:43.205
Yuriko.

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:47.904
There's still some left to drink.

00:05:48.914 --> 00:05:49.938
Captain...

00:05:50.916 --> 00:05:56.821
Thank you. Captain, I...
I may never see you again.

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:58.947
But, I'll never forget...

00:05:59.058 --> 00:05:59.990
Yuriko!

00:06:01.026 --> 00:06:02.220
...what a good man you were.

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:19.478
He's what?!

00:06:19.478 --> 00:06:22.345
You mean he isn't coming back?!

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:26.252
And after all the
worrying we've been doing.

00:06:26.252 --> 00:06:29.221
Let's go! I won't feel right
till I've popped him one!

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:30.322
Make that two!

00:06:31.123 --> 00:06:33.057
Can't you calm down? Please?

00:06:35.427 --> 00:06:39.227
There are times people
just want to be alone.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:45.327
Then you're saying the
captain was serious about this?

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:46.961
I can't believe it...

00:06:47.239 --> 00:06:48.729
Poor Mr. Tylor...

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:50.808
What do you think?

00:06:51.243 --> 00:06:54.576
I know how he feels. There are
times I want to be alone, too.

00:06:55.181 --> 00:06:58.378
But, it's not like him.
Being all alone.

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:00.916
It's just not like him...

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:06.089
After all, aren't we here
for when he feels that way?

00:07:06.525 --> 00:07:10.928
You only live once, so don't live
according to someone else's rules.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:13.664
Do what you want
the way you want to.

00:07:15.367 --> 00:07:16.891
He asked me
to tell you all that.

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:36.646
CAPTAIN!!!

00:07:40.492 --> 00:07:42.960
A toast, to Tylor's discharge.

00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:48.092
Admiral?

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:50.703
Could it be that you're
feeling a little lonely...

00:07:50.703 --> 00:07:53.604
...because you won't have him
around to be angry at anymore?

00:07:54.874 --> 00:07:56.171
No, it's not that...

00:07:56.242 --> 00:07:59.473
It's not that. I was just thinking
about something I heard once.

00:08:00.179 --> 00:08:01.373
About monkey tribes.

00:08:06.318 --> 00:08:10.311
Monkeys create very organized
tribes, with a leader at the top.

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:12.856
But, once every few
years without fail...

00:08:12.925 --> 00:08:15.587
...a heretic monkey
will appear in the tribe.

00:08:15.728 --> 00:08:17.059
A heretic monkey?

00:08:17.196 --> 00:08:21.155
This heretic will leave his
tribe and try to join another.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:25.336
The monkeys of this new tribe
will try to keep it out...

00:08:25.404 --> 00:08:28.532
...literally beating
it until it's bloody.

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:33.279
Ah, so even monkey societies
have strays like Tylor.

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:37.181
However, those strays are a
vital element to their survival.

00:08:37.349 --> 00:08:38.680
A vital element?

00:08:38.751 --> 00:08:43.586
The reason is that the heretics
keep them from inbreeding too much.

00:08:43.656 --> 00:08:46.625
It keeps the tribal bloodline
from growing too thick.

00:08:46.759 --> 00:08:50.752
The heretic monkey is necessary
for the tribe's survival.

00:08:50.829 --> 00:08:54.233
You're saying these heretics are
born from a providence of nature?

00:08:54.233 --> 00:09:00.673
Yes, and Tylor may be the heretic
for our own military society.

00:09:00.673 --> 00:09:04.404
Admiral, are you suggesting
that the military needs Tylor?

00:09:22.695 --> 00:09:24.492
What's wrong, Admiral?

00:09:32.071 --> 00:09:34.665
The heretic is the vital
link in any group.

00:09:34.873 --> 00:09:39.003
But I still don't know
if Tylor is the one.

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:49.115
You want me to be the
captain of the Aso?!

00:09:49.355 --> 00:09:50.122
Exactly.

00:09:50.122 --> 00:09:51.350
And not just that.

00:09:51.523 --> 00:09:54.458
You will also simultaneously be
promoted to the rank of captain.

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:55.990
Captain...

00:09:56.161 --> 00:09:59.892
We can't very well have the Aso
commanded by a mere lieutenant.

00:10:00.699 --> 00:10:03.099
The Aso is our newest cruiser...

00:10:03.168 --> 00:10:06.968
...representing the combined talent
of the Space Force's design staff.

00:10:07.139 --> 00:10:10.040
We had intended for Tylor
to command her...

00:10:10.109 --> 00:10:12.805
...but I'm sure you're well
aware of last month's events.

00:10:13.479 --> 00:10:14.104
Yes, sir.

00:10:14.413 --> 00:10:17.007
I have no desire to discuss
what can't be undone.

00:10:18.384 --> 00:10:22.377
In any case, I feel a man like
you deserves command of the Aso.

00:10:22.654 --> 00:10:24.679
Sir! I'm honored, sir.

00:10:24.957 --> 00:10:27.983
I'll leave the selection
of the crew up to you.

00:10:29.061 --> 00:10:32.765
If you wish, you can even have
your old crew from the Soyokaze.

00:10:32.765 --> 00:10:35.791
With the exception of
Capt. Yuriko Star...

00:10:35.868 --> 00:10:39.031
...who has been deputy commander
of Intel Ops since last month.

00:10:39.204 --> 00:10:41.138
You cannot request her.

00:10:41.306 --> 00:10:41.795
Sir!

00:10:41.874 --> 00:10:44.968
The Aso's launch ceremony
is in three days.

00:10:45.110 --> 00:10:47.203
We have high hopes
for you, Captain Yamamoto.

00:10:47.579 --> 00:10:52.107
Sir! As a member of the
United Planets Space Force...

00:10:52.184 --> 00:10:55.153
...I stand ready to sacrifice
my body, my flesh, my life...

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:57.916
...to successfully complete
this task you've assigned!

00:10:59.058 --> 00:11:01.727
Then begin your
preparations at once!

00:11:01.727 --> 00:11:02.887
Understood, sir!

00:11:03.228 --> 00:11:05.924
The cruiser Aso...
Captain Yamamoto...

00:11:06.465 --> 00:11:09.366
I understand perfectly.

00:11:21.113 --> 00:11:25.573
It looks like Captain Yamamoto's
calling in the old Soyokaze crew.

00:11:26.118 --> 00:11:26.607
Yeah.

00:11:27.186 --> 00:11:30.246
Doesn't it bother you?
You were one of the Soyokaze's...

00:11:32.124 --> 00:11:34.251
I was one of the Soyokaze's crew.

00:11:34.927 --> 00:11:36.895
But that's behind me now.

00:11:37.596 --> 00:11:38.858
Behind you now?

00:11:39.798 --> 00:11:42.528
So, what are the other
Soyokaze crew members doing now?

00:11:42.935 --> 00:11:46.268
Doing what Captain Tylor
asked them to do.

00:11:46.605 --> 00:11:49.130
Each one took the path
they wanted to take.

00:12:45.898 --> 00:12:46.592
Go away!

00:12:50.536 --> 00:12:51.434
Just go away!

00:13:43.322 --> 00:13:45.483
Shall we get started, Harumi?

00:13:45.557 --> 00:13:46.524
Yes, Doctor.

00:13:48.227 --> 00:13:51.526
United Planets Space Force.
Message from Captain Yamamoto.

00:13:52.064 --> 00:13:53.656
Hmm... Well, now...

00:13:53.932 --> 00:13:55.126
What is it, Doctor?

00:13:55.334 --> 00:13:57.564
It's from Mr. Yamamoto. Here.

00:13:58.036 --> 00:14:02.541
We've been asked to reenlist and
report to the Aso... Is this?

00:14:02.541 --> 00:14:06.545
Well, looks like Mr. Yamamoto
is doing well for himself.

00:14:06.545 --> 00:14:07.637
I'd say so.

00:14:07.713 --> 00:14:09.681
Harumi, I'm canceling
the operation.

00:14:09.881 --> 00:14:10.848
Yes, Doctor.

00:14:38.043 --> 00:14:41.570
SPACE CRUISER ASO
LAUNCH CEREMONY

00:15:05.771 --> 00:15:11.004
Well, Admiral, the Aso's
launch ceremony will begin soon.

00:15:11.109 --> 00:15:16.012
Yes. The 1731st ship
of the Mifune fleet.

00:15:19.351 --> 00:15:21.285
Almost time, Captain Star.

00:15:21.453 --> 00:15:21.976
Yes.

00:15:22.621 --> 00:15:28.582
But I thought the Soyokaze crew
had split up to do what they wanted.

00:15:29.094 --> 00:15:31.062
Why'd they come onto the Aso?

00:15:31.263 --> 00:15:32.457
Oh, here.

00:15:32.831 --> 00:15:34.025
Thank you, Lieutenant.

00:15:37.302 --> 00:15:40.703
Probably because this was also
something they wanted to do.

00:15:40.806 --> 00:15:44.298
Some set out on a new journey,
and others stay behind, huh?

00:15:46.044 --> 00:15:49.343
It feels strange... Sort of
happy and sad at the same time.

00:15:49.748 --> 00:15:53.047
But everyone chose to
come back on their own.

00:15:53.185 --> 00:15:55.119
Mr. Yamamoto must be so happy.

00:15:55.187 --> 00:15:58.122
Getting a brand-new cruiser
for his first command...

00:15:58.256 --> 00:15:59.484
That's an incredible success.

00:16:00.325 --> 00:16:02.316
You should consider
how hard it was for him.

00:16:02.828 --> 00:16:05.729
Mr. Yamamoto had to put up
with a lot of suffering...

00:16:05.797 --> 00:16:07.697
...and he had to wait so long.

00:16:07.866 --> 00:16:10.460
Yeah, I guess you're right.

00:16:11.103 --> 00:16:11.831
Exactly.

00:16:15.507 --> 00:16:16.997
Now, then...

00:16:17.876 --> 00:16:20.845
All sections,
commence final checks!

00:16:20.946 --> 00:16:23.437
Dropship bay, standing by.

00:16:23.782 --> 00:16:24.544
Right!

00:16:24.883 --> 00:16:26.544
No problems here!

00:16:26.752 --> 00:16:27.514
Right!

00:16:27.686 --> 00:16:30.154
Hangar bay,
ready and standing by!

00:16:30.422 --> 00:16:31.150
Right!

00:16:31.223 --> 00:16:33.418
Medical room,
ready for anything!

00:16:33.592 --> 00:16:34.354
Right!

00:16:34.493 --> 00:16:36.688
Communications systems,
all operational!

00:16:36.828 --> 00:16:37.658
Right!

00:16:37.763 --> 00:16:40.630
Engines and navigation
systems, nominal!

00:16:41.032 --> 00:16:41.521
Right!

00:16:41.933 --> 00:16:43.833
Toilets and baths,
clean and shiny!

00:16:43.902 --> 00:16:45.631
Breasts and bottoms,
clean and shiny!

00:16:47.072 --> 00:16:48.767
All set over here, too.

00:16:49.474 --> 00:16:53.672
Right! Right! RIGHT!!!

00:16:54.012 --> 00:16:56.810
Everything's ready!

00:16:57.115 --> 00:16:58.776
That idiot's really
enjoying himself.

00:16:58.850 --> 00:17:01.114
They say pigs can climb trees
if you flatter them enough.

00:17:03.155 --> 00:17:06.488
Right! And now,
as this vessel's captain...

00:17:09.928 --> 00:17:11.122
...your orders, sir!

00:17:11.797 --> 00:17:12.491
Move out!

00:18:23.068 --> 00:18:24.535
What's happening?!

00:18:41.019 --> 00:18:42.680
The Soyokaze! It can't be!

00:18:43.622 --> 00:18:46.557
The reports coming in from
the Aso have all been cut.

00:18:46.925 --> 00:18:48.654
All hell's probably
going to break loose now.

00:18:49.961 --> 00:18:53.624
I don't! You mean you were
all planning this from the start?!

00:18:53.798 --> 00:18:56.164
Each of us on our own
decided to do this.

00:18:56.234 --> 00:18:57.098
On your own?

00:18:57.903 --> 00:18:59.962
Right, just like
the captain said.

00:19:00.238 --> 00:19:03.469
We each just did what we
wanted the way we wanted to.

00:19:03.675 --> 00:19:04.471
That's all.

00:19:07.145 --> 00:19:07.736
Here.

00:19:16.054 --> 00:19:18.113
Bon voyage, Captain!

00:19:28.366 --> 00:19:29.162
Thank you.

00:19:30.035 --> 00:19:31.603
Paco-Paco did THAT?!

00:19:31.603 --> 00:19:32.070
Yes.

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:32.203
Yes.
Paco-Paco...
That's strange, even for you!

00:19:32.203 --> 00:19:36.037
Paco-Paco...
That's strange, even for you!

00:19:36.374 --> 00:19:38.274
Now that he's back...

00:19:38.343 --> 00:19:41.244
...we can't underestimate the
United Planets Space Force.

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:43.341
We must be very careful now.

00:19:43.415 --> 00:19:46.043
Shia Has, you're
still so shortsighted.

00:19:47.085 --> 00:19:49.254
He may be in the
Space Force for now...

00:19:49.254 --> 00:19:51.415
...but how long will
he be content with that?

00:19:52.023 --> 00:19:55.356
His capacities may be
far greater than we imagine.

00:19:55.493 --> 00:19:56.323
I know!

00:19:57.395 --> 00:20:02.025
Ru Baraba Dom, I command you!
Bring Paco-Paco before me once more!

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:07.905
I just suddenly feel
like seeing him again.

00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:10.501
Shia Has! YOU get him!

00:20:13.712 --> 00:20:15.373
And now!

00:20:15.680 --> 00:20:20.049
Commence recovery of Yuriko!

00:20:20.452 --> 00:20:21.942
Begin operation!

00:20:27.325 --> 00:20:30.385
The heretic...
The vital link in any group!

00:20:31.429 --> 00:20:32.555
You idiot!

00:20:32.697 --> 00:20:36.133
What are you people in Intel
Ops doing?! Who's responsible...

00:20:37.469 --> 00:20:39.767
Oh, if only I
could meet him once...

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:43.130
The irresponsible captain.

00:20:44.442 --> 00:20:46.603
Engines, full power!

00:20:47.345 --> 00:20:49.540
Full speed ahead!

00:21:22.514 --> 00:21:26.450
Justy Ueki Tylor, age twenty...
Harumi, my dear?

00:21:26.685 --> 00:21:27.447
Yes, sir?

00:21:27.519 --> 00:21:31.979
I think there may be
hope for mankind after all.

00:21:32.223 --> 00:21:32.882
Yes, sir.

00:21:40.765 --> 00:21:43.290
LET'S GO!!!

00:22:05.423 --> 00:22:10.053
AND SO LONG AS THE
IRRESPONSIBLE EXPLORE
UNKNOWN LANDS,
WE NEED NEVER FEAR...

00:22:23.541 --> 00:22:26.644
All he has to do is just...
Machi o Aitsu ga Aruiteru dake de

00:22:26.644 --> 00:22:29.738
...walk around downtown.
Machi o Aitsu ga Aruiteru dake de

00:22:30.248 --> 00:22:33.718
He's a playful man who catches...
Nandemo Ki o Hiku Ochame na Yatsu sa

